OCR libraries (compiled into Kimochi)
-------------------------------------

meikiocr (crate from https://github.com/hamstu/kimochi-meikiocr), Apache-2.0.
A Rust port of MeikiOCR (https://github.com/rtr46/meikiocr, Apache-2.0),
upstream revision 52aa607ecdc1038c7bf390f37cd9a8b306e8a08a; its
preprocessing and postprocessing were adapted from meikiocr/ocr.py. The
Apache License 2.0 is in LICENSE-APACHE.

mangaocr (crate from https://github.com/hamstu/kimochi-mangaocr),
GPL-3.0-only. Native Rust inference and page grouping for:
  - Manga OCR: https://github.com/kha-white/manga-ocr (Apache-2.0); the
    Apache License 2.0 is in LICENSE-APACHE.
  - Comic Text Detector: https://github.com/dmMaze/comic-text-detector
    (GPL-3.0), source revision 440b978563c71b758e31aaa315d100faba1efa2f.
    Because the detector is ported from it, the crate as a whole is
    GPL-3.0-only.
Test manga imagery is not bundled or licensed by this project.

The licence and notice files of both crates travel inside the app, in its
meikiocr/ and mangaocr/ resource directories.


Google Lens OCR (src-tauri/src/google_lens.rs)
----------------------------------------------

Kimochi's Google Lens engine is a Rust port of the Google Lens engine in
owocr by AuroraWright (https://github.com/AuroraWright/owocr, owocr/ocr.py,
class GoogleLens, revision 5ddee7961a9b5b4a50fa0b2afc41f9eea72bb5d5),
GPL-3.0-only. The request it sends, the endpoint and headers, the image size
limit and the reading of text and geometry from the response follow owocr.
Its protobuf messages are a hand-written subset of the Lens overlay protocol
definitions from Chromium (third_party/lens_server_proto), which owocr
generates its bindings from; Copyright The Chromium Authors, BSD-3-Clause.
No Google software is included. When you choose Google Lens, captures are
sent to Google's Lens service and are subject to Google's terms.


