Engine icons
------------

The small pictures beside each OCR and dictionary engine in Settings and the
welcome guide are in frontend/assets/engine-icons/ (README there):

  - yomitan.svg: Yomitan's icon, ext/images/yomitan-icon.svg from
    https://github.com/yomidevs/yomitan (release 26.8.24.0),
    GPL-3.0-or-later; a viewBox added so it scales.
  - yomitan-api.svg: the same Yomitan icon with a curly-brace badge added by
    Kimochi (the Yomitan API), a modified version under GPL-3.0-or-later.
  - hachidori.png: Hachidori's icon, icons/hachidori-128.png from
    https://github.com/bee-san/hachidori (release 0.3.0), GPL-3.0-or-later,
    resized to 64 px.
  - tenten.svg: 10ten's icon, images/10ten.svg from
    https://github.com/birchill/10ten-ja-reader (release v1.28.0),
    GPL-3.0-or-later; a faint edge added so it shows on dark grounds.
  - kimochi-cloud.svg: Kimochi's own icon (branding/), for Cloud OCR.
  - google-lens.svg: the Google Lens icon as published by Google
    (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Google_Lens_Icon.svg, marked
    there as public domain), cropped to its artwork.
  - windows.svg: the four-pane Windows logo, drawn for Kimochi, for OneOCR
    (the OCR in Windows Snipping Tool).
Apple Live Text, MeikiOCR and Manga OCR are shown with a lucide glyph
(ScanText, ISC) or a monogram, not a logo.

